  "decision": "The full patch removes only a local `panelId` binding from the upstream modern autocomplete modal-ownership spec; it leaves the production implementation untouched. This is a test-only upstream cleanup, not a package source change. The add-on has its own legacy autocomplete implementation and tests; its trigger still performs the aria-owns reads and removes/sets them as appropriate. Do not treat deletion of this upstream test statement as proof that the read is generally side-effect-free, or as a behavioral/accessibility qualification.",
